        <div type="bibliography">
          <p>
             The inscription was noted in A. R. No. 337 of 1922<!-- has to be adjusted to the @target --> and first published by J. Ramayya Pantulu (<bibl rend="omitname"><ptr target="bib:RamayyaPantulu1948_01"/><citedRange unit="page">336</citedRange><citedRange unit="item">616</citedRange></bibl>). K. M. Sastri re-edits that edition and provides a summary: <cit><quote>Refers to a gift of pannasa to brahmins of the Bhāradwāja gōtra and contains the imprecation that he who acts unjustly against it will incur the sin of having killed a thousand brahmins at Baranasi</quote><bibl rend="omitname"><ptr target="bib:Sastri1969_01"/><citedRange unit="page">335</citedRange><citedRange unit="item">73</citedRange></bibl></cit>.
          </p>
